outputs are new files under this task's evidence directory. Final unit fixtures use
TMPDIR within the owned checkout and are removed by unittest cleanup.

Outputs: summary.json, trials.json/csv, arms.json/csv, paired.json/csv. Every output
is labeled DEVELOPMENT ONLY for an explicit --allow-development invocation. Strict
mode requires passed matrix and trial records, clean committed manifest/trial flags,
matching source/runtime/binary/build receipt identities, consistent probe bytes and
compatible measurement provenance. Host/idle/sampling/backing-device protocol
identity prevents pooling incompatible matrices. Development groups remain separate.
The analyzer's own SHA-256 and each trial input's SHA-256 are recorded in JSON.

Accounting and validity:
- Primary memory: dedicated cgroup memory.current sampled peak, mean, endpoints and
  trapezoid byte-seconds. Full host phase start->workload_complete is separate from
  the fixed common idle window. Default idle offset/window are 5s/20s; this legacy
  10s-idle smoke requires the explicitly recorded development override 2s/5s.
- Idle starts at max(vm idle_start.received_host_monotonic_ns)+offset and ends
  strictly before both guest idle_end records. Host/PSS samples must bracket it;
  gaps over max-gap (default 1.5s), missing core values, identity changes, counter
  resets, malformed records and failed correctness/provenance checks reject analysis.
  Window endpoints use local linear interpolation, not extrapolation or zero fill.
  Sampled peaks and trapezoid integrals do not establish unsampled true peaks.
- Cgroup CPU usage/user/system microsecond deltas and memory.stat pgfault/pgmajfault
  deltas are computed separately for both windows. Faults remain counters, not bytes.
- VMM aggregate PSS is a separate mapped-memory view; shared RSS is never summed.
  Full-trial PSS is explicitly unavailable when startup is not bracketed. Idle-only
  per-VMM own minflt/majflt and /proc/io deltas are separate views and are not added
  to cgroup, guest or physical-I/O counters. Optional read failures remain NA+reason.
- Host meminfo is explicitly a whole-host/unrelated-workload view. It is not added
  to PSS or cgroup charges. Guest AnonPages/Cached/MemTotal and available other fields
  are actual probe phase endpoints, not invented common-window guest samples.
- Physical I/O prefers manifest.backing_device.physical_major_minor; explicit
  --physical-device overrides it. Legacy fallback resolves the current matrix-output
  filesystem's /sys/dev/block partition parent. Moved observations need recorded
  provenance or an explicit device. This smoke resolves filesystem8:3 to physical8:0.
- io.stat layers are recorded individually and never summed. Missing initial device
  counters/read errors yield NA+reason for that delta, while valid memory/CPU results
  survive. The selected physical cumulative counter at window end uses immediate
  valid brackets independently, includes pre-phase work since fresh cgroup creation,
  and is labeled separately. Raw edge values/times and read errors are retained.
- CreateVM/readback durations, guest CPU/fault counters, instrumented phase timing,
  reporting traffic/descriptors, file st_blocks allocation and pool backing fields
  are retained as available. Probe timings include sampling/hash/canary work and are
  not pure storage latency. Reporting traffic is not unique freed bytes; st_blocks
  sums are per-file allocation observations, not unique physical extents.
- CSV annotations expose window boundaries, the selected device and unavailable
  metric/layer reasons. Missing numeric cells remain empty, never zero-filled.
- Block pairs are original->disk, disk->reclaim, ext4-block->pmem and
  ext4-reclaim->combined. Differences are target-minus-baseline with medians/min/max
  and counts. No SquashFS/ext4 format difference is attributed to pmem. No savings
  percentage or paper claim is generated.

